/-!
# Native sphere field arithmetic in genuine punctured scalar germs

All native meromorphic sphere functions have regular representatives
on sufficiently small punctured coordinate neighborhoods.  Their
actual addition, multiplication, negation, total inverse, and division
therefore agree with ordinary scalar arithmetic as punctured germs,
with no pole or nonzero-denominator assumptions in the resulting
formulas.  Constants agree pointwise everywhere.

The resulting injective ring homomorphism takes values in the actual
ring of scalar punctured germs.  Polynomial and quotient formulas are
proved for arbitrary native meromorphic functions and arbitrary complex
polynomials, rather than assumed for a chosen rational presentation.
-/
